{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1152913-stranger-covenants","id":1152913,"title":"Stranger Covenants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-25T13:39:05-07:00","id":1152913,"title":"Stranger Covenants","content":"So, I'm putting this concept together for a early 19th century American setting. Several smaller, but rapidly growing, towns with a single Kindred leadership... though not a very unified one. The cities will be pretty industrial and have no closeby neighbours, not other cities and no Native American nations, and their main sources of trade are between them and through the pretty large port of the port-town (which is also the largest one).<br /> <br /> So, for covenants I'm thinking I want them to be similar to, but different, from the ones in the books. Local color so to speak. No Carthians of course, too early and too... dunno. Difficult to get the right feeling for with the setting.<br /> So, with that in mind I'm kinda wondering if people have any good ideas or pieces of inspiration they'd like to share? Pet 'extra' covenants that I should consider?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T17:52:34-07:00","id":1152988,"title":"","content":"Extra covenants depend on what role you want them to serve. Do you want an alien group that the players will have to work to understand the world view of? An enemy they'll need to fight? Possible alies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T21:45:58-07:00","id":1153057,"title":"","content":"Well, in a game played right all covenants should hold possible allies, enemies, resources and enigmas so any of that works. Right now I'm more looking for inspiration and ideas, twists to the base covenants or strange new ones perhaps.<br /> <br /> The best thought I've had so far is to perhaps throw in a strange Coil for the Ordo and make it a central part of their local philosophy, perhaps the Coil of Zirnitra, while at the same time removing all recognition for the Coil of the Wyrm (it isn't officially taught and knowing it is not recognized for the purposes of rank but it isn't forbidden... just not viewed very well). That's the mechanics difference of course, with their philosophy being rather heavily focused on studying various other supernatural beings and taking their gifts for themselves in various ways.<br /> <br /> That... is it so far though, and I'm still not entirely sold on that part.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T04:31:41-07:00","id":1153111,"title":"","content":"The Invitus is probably planing for the long term here so they will seek to grab things that will give reliable income in ten years time or more. If you have The Dance Macabre look at Brethren of the Hundred Faces, The Children of the Thorns, The Nemites and maybe The Society of the Accord for wild cards your players might not know. You might want to save the Circle for the second act as with no natives there's unlikely to be much tolerance for pagin faths, alternatively you could have them be an occult society with an intellectual flavour and have the Ordo be still trying to standardise its methodology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T11:36:53-07:00","id":1153768,"title":"","content":"Alright, so, some thinking and reading done I've come up with a few bits and least. Covenants haven't been ironed out entirely but some bits have been put down.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Invictus </u></b>- The largest, and also most influential, which is pretty standard. They literally tax kindred, then use the money they garner to create businesses and industries in the cities that in turn are used to manipulate the region and the citizens. Among their leadership the maxim &quot;Money is power made manifest.&quot; is used. While this situation does cause some grumbling the fact that they have developed racks at the request of covenant leaders, granted various boons to up-and-comers and so successfully manipulated managed to entice people from overseas to immigrate to the local colonies has made them very difficult to oppose.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Church of the First Saints (Circle)</u></b> - There's a church on the edge of one of the smaller, and also very poor, villages. That entire village consists of the members of the Circle, their ghouls and unghouled thralls, all of which worship Lilith. Their faith's christian veneer is an intentional camouflage, the name a joke the local Mother came up with, and their organization fairly loose. Unusually enough this has resulted in them managing a pretty cordial relationship with the Lancea Sanctum, stretching so far as to mean that some of the Circle's members attending the weekly mass.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lancea et Sanctum</u></b> - An underground hall, eight feet high and ten yards on each side, is where the Lancea hold their Sunday Mass each week. They're public and political, maintaining and running three of the largest local racks and allow anyone who attends on Sundays, and who acts responsibly, feed there. Their local philosophy is much akin to what it is elsewhere but a lot of their focus is on finding guilt before they act and as such they have a fair number of people skilled in Empathy as well as have rituals focused around truth; knowing it, compelling people to speak it and punishing lies. Due to the nature of those Prayers (the local term for their rituals) their leaders often serve as judges or arbiters for trials or other conflicts between local kindred.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Ordo Dracul</u></b> - Chasing the Dragon, that is the goal of the local Ordo. Gaining insight, understanding, is their local mantra and as such anything that provides them the ability to perceive or understand is treasured. Many members, even those from clans that do not provide it, learn Auspex and they have methods for doing so that do not require the drinking of kindred blood as well as a large number of devotions based on it. A local Coil, not fully developed, exists which sharpens and develops the senses of a kindred and it is very well thought of. Conversely the Coil of the Wyrm is viewed as quite low due to the fact that, in many ways, requires the loss of faculties and awareness they locally prize and this disregard is so pronounced that it is not even recognized for the purposes of local titles.<br /> <br /> All that said... as you can see it's still pretty poor on &quot;twists&quot; for several of them and I've yet to be able to make a decision in regards to a fifth covenant so any ideas or suggestions would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1734,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","user":"Asaram","date":". 10-28-2017, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T14:50:35-07:00","id":1154231,"title":"","content":"I tried to find a common thread between your examples and I think I've noticed something. Lancea et Sanctum put their trust in a higher power (Theban Sorcery) so it can lead them to truth. Ordo Dracul, misotheist as always, refine their senses, Disciplines and skills to do the same. The remaining Covenants represent an opposite. Circle of the Crone uses deception for religious reasons, and it's safe to assume the Invictus lie and deceive for personal gain. A fifth Covenant could represent an alternate approach, trucking with memetic hazards, using a resource that subtly rewrites history, or something in the same vein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T16:32:45-07:00","id":1154248,"title":"","content":"Oh, hey! I did not consider that but you are right. Unintentional theme-setting here. That is rather amusing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for memetic hazards or alternate history... I'm not sure what you mean. Could you elaborate? It sounds like you've got ideas that, honestly, fit my tastes very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T17:11:50-07:00","id":1154257,"title":"","content":"Baced of Teatimes observation I would look at Brethren of the Hundred Faces for their unique take on truth or The Nemites for their hypocrisy both are in Dance Macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T17:35:18-07:00","id":1154261,"title":"","content":"The idea is to introduce a factor that puts a spin on themes of other Covenants, regardless of its origin. <br /> <br /> When I say &quot;memetic hazards&quot; I mean all phenomena that interfere with the mind. If we stay within Requiem's canon, we have Dominate which can implant false memories, and Malkavia disease which is a contagious insanity that brings forth both delusions and strange insight. If we go beyond Requiem, there are at least two kinds of Demons that may successfully lie even to supernatural powers, and maybe even trade their knowledge for services (you can make a Covenant of Infernalists). Then there's the God-Machine and all the strangeness it creates. Video recordings that overwrite subject's memory, sentient shared hallucinations that affect subjects at will, infectious delusions that change their subject's beliefs (Holy Engineers Covenant have a different focus, but they represent this strangeness well). You can tie those to any other Gameline, but you don't need to do even that. They might just be a strange thing that happens.<br /> <br /> So, if a Theban ritual reads peoples' intentions instead of finding objective truth, these phenomena may easily mislead it. Also, even a master of Auspex may become wary if they fear they get false sensory input. Whoever harnesses these phenomena for their benefit gains a massive advantage, that they may use to compete with other Covenants.<br /> <br /> As for alternate histories, my first thought was a phenomenon that temporarily replaces people, objects and places with a version from another history. Their, properties, abilities and memories are different, but they're not false. Those who exploit this power may leave notes for themselves, so their alter-egos know what to accomplish and who not to trust. Alternatively, a phenomenon where a lie repeated enough literally becomes true. You would need to decide what is the extent and limitations of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:14:21-07:00","id":1154428,"title":"","content":"While a tempting idea it sounds more like an antagonist group, attacking the foundation of several Covenants so directly.<br /> The approach however does bring an idea to mind. The Invictus and the Lancea are both very intent on the real world, they're political and practical. The Dragons and the Circle are not, they're intent on the spiritual or intellectual and only pay attention to the real world when they have to in order to pursue or protect their work.<br /> <br /> I'm consider if maybe a faction that lives outside the cities, a sort of loosely connected &quot;Hobo network&quot; sort of thing, might be made interesting somehow. Interested in the physical but not having much in the way of it, craving the spiritual and it's ideals but not having the freedom to seek it. It fits rather well in my head but... not sure how to make such a faction interesting, other than providing them a number of devotions that allow them to live in such a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:50:30-07:00","id":1154443,"title":"","content":"Your idea seems pretty close to the classic tension between &quot;Haves&quot; and &quot;Have-nots&quot;. You may decide to make the fifth Covenant second-class citizens, that are occasionally useful for those in power, be it for dirty work, their unique abilities or as scapegoats. The idea is that leading Covenants can afford to follow a greater cause, while the others are struggling to survive. There's a lot of material to take inspiration from. Cursed Bloodlines like Morbus, Neglatu and their Revenants, Vampires afflicted with Malkavia, Caitiff and their sympathizers. I know Caitiff are from Masquerade, but you can get a lot of inspiration out of it as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T11:49:55-07:00","id":1154453,"title":"","content":"Yes, I was envisioning something like that. The group starting as outcasts of various sorts, those who for one reason or another fell outside of the existing covenants, but then they organized and, in time, grew to be a troublesome sort of group that for better or worse stands outside of the structure.<br /> It wouldn't be a potent group by any means, they'd be subsisting on animals and the few farmers living outside of the reach of the existing domains, but it might have a very varied and resourceful group of members.<br /> <br /> As for curses, that is a rather interesting twist... there'd have to be some way to make it universal though, applied to all members rather. First thing that comes to mind is a wishing well that grants 1 dot of merits at most, maybe for a month, but also afflicts the person who made the wish with a personalized tradeoff... except for vampires it's always X thing? Question would be what, and if there might be some better way to do it than a wishing well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T11:51:19-07:00","id":1154454,"title":"","content":"That makes sense to me. At the frontier, while there is less surveillance and law enforcement, there are also less people to feed from. The higher-ups have their dedicated herds and the rest feed off the dregs and hope not to get caught. Also, how do Caitiff work with the idea that each &quot;Clan&quot; is one of a number of occult species that experienced convergent evolution?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd by OP themselves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T12:04:35-07:00","id":1154459,"title":"","content":"Well, Caitiff in CofD are simply (as per standard) simply those who do not know their own lineage. While this will, in time, be rectified in most situations this is far from a true given. Some might, for example, commit diablerie early on (during a frenzy perhaps) and so have more than one unique discipline. They might have banes that resemble, or even copy, part of the clan banes of others and so on.<br /> <br /> In short, it is possible to not know your clan, but as it is extremely rare not to have one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:35:34-07:00","id":1154494,"title":"","content":"Having a literal curse is not really necessary. Belonging to the fifth Covenant might mean being tainted by association - at least in the eyes of mainstream Covenants. However, having a magic wishing well that grants boons for a price is a fantastic idea. Especially if the desperate stand to gain most but lose least in the process. This would explain why more privileged Vampires aren't eager to use it. My mind went to Goblin Contracts from Changeling: the Lost 1st Edition. If you haven't read them, they were agreements with aspects of reality, sealed through Faerie magic. Some neat examples include:<br /> <br /> 1. Disguise one object as another. Once the effect lapses everyone you deceived will know you did it.<br /> 2. Predict the future. Forget what you said and become mentally unstable for a time.<br /> 3. Avoid injury from any one source. It returns to you on top of everything else when you're next wounded.<br /> 4. Escape any captivity. In return, another enemy will know where you now are.<br /> <br /> ...or the well could temporarily rewrite your past to give you an extra Skill or Merit, but it rewrites something random permanently. *Being cheeky*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:48:02-07:00","id":1154501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1152913-stranger-covenants?p=1154459#post1154459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Caitiff in CofD are simply (as per standard) simply those who do not know their own lineage. While this will, in time, be rectified in most situations this is far from a true given. Some might, for example, commit diablerie early on (during a frenzy perhaps) and so have more than one unique discipline. They might have banes that resemble, or even copy, part of the clan banes of others and so on.<br /> <br /> In short, it is possible to not know your clan, but as it is extremely rare not to have one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forget Blood Sympathy. Pinging it once or twice might not be clear enough, but eventually you'll be able to piece it together from that if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Vampires can also pick out clan by tasting the vampire's blood, if they know the taste (pg. 91). Auspex 2 could also do it, debatably.<br /> <br /> While it may be possible to not know your clan, I don't expect that to last very long if you want to find out. Or if anyone else has any reason to try and find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T15:46:24-07:00","id":1154532,"title":"","content":"I'm actually considering a faerie-tale from where I grew up as a possible inspiration. It wasn't a well so much as a dried up spring of old. Long story short a farmer kept throwing shiny rocks into it and kept getting food through rather implausible means, the twist in the end of course being that you should not try to 'steal' food through such means.<br /> <br /> What I'm thinking here is a similar thing, a mostly dried up spring that will grant whoever gives it something (undecided) food for a period. The downside then being, perhaps, that they gain a social flaw (Ostracised) or similar for the same duration. For the kindred of course this results in them gaining one dot of Herd through seriously circumspect coincidences, lasting maybe a month or so, and having serious issues actually joining the established covenants.<br /> Of course, without this 'blessing' it would be difficult for them to even subsist, let alone get their stuff together enough to be allowed in their door once they've been associated with the 'outcasts'.<br /> <br /> Either of you have better ideas or suggestions for how to twist it? Or what is 'sacrificed'?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T15:50:07-07:00","id":1155208,"title":"","content":"I confess I'm running out of ideas, but I must ask: Are you planning a chronicle for specific players, or are you making a setting as a creative exercise? If the former, you could ask them what they want out of a game and base your decision on that. If the latter, do you have a theme you'd like to apply to your setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T17:53:39-07:00","id":1155232,"title":"","content":"More of a creative exercise and, honestly, you've given me a fair number of ideas already. While the city in itself is far from done, same for the covenants in general, the &quot;fifth covenant&quot; is actually coming together pretty well. I just haven't been able to put it all down and post it here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T18:09:12-07:00","id":1155235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1152913-stranger-covenants?p=1154428#post1154428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a tempting idea it sounds more like an antagonist group, attacking the foundation of several Covenants so directly.<br /> The approach however does bring an idea to mind. The Invictus and the Lancea are both very intent on the real world, they're political and practical. The Dragons and the Circle are not, they're intent on the spiritual or intellectual and only pay attention to the real world when they have to in order to pursue or protect their work.<br /> <br /> I'm consider if maybe a faction that lives outside the cities, a sort of loosely connected &quot;Hobo network&quot; sort of thing, might be made interesting somehow. Interested in the physical but not having much in the way of it, craving the spiritual and it's ideals but not having the freedom to seek it. It fits rather well in my head but... not sure how to make such a faction interesting, other than providing them a number of devotions that allow them to live in such a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the Gallows Post in a land with railways/steamboats to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T18:22:39-07:00","id":1155239,"title":"","content":"Indeed it does and I will admit I took a few to reread a bit about them, but the concept has veered away from that concept now. While there will still be a Gallows Post feel to some parts of it the core of the covenants will be a little more philosophy/ideology still, rather than just making sure everyone is fed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}